        "topic": "Accounting Equation",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2005",
        "question_text": "<p>The assets of a business are \u20b515,000 and the liabilities are \u20b55,000. What is the owner's equity?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The accounting equation is $Assets = Liabilities + Owner's\\ Equity$.<br>Rearranging, $Owner's\\ Equity = Assets - Liabilities$.<br>Thus, $Owner's\\ Equity = \u20b515,000 - \u20b55,000 = \u20b510,000$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
